Motor vehicle means a vehicle having two (2) or more load-bearing wheels of a kind required to be registered under the laws of this state relating to motor vehicles designed primarily for operation upon the public streets, roads, and highways and driven by power other than muscular power. The term includes a trailer drawn by or attached to such a vehicle and also includes without limitation a low speed vehicle.
Owner means the owner of the subject real property or premises as shown on the deed records of Walker County, Georgia, the occupant in possession including a tenant or lessee, and any person designated by the owner or occupant to manage the premises. When known to the enforcement officer, the term "owner" also includes the person to whom the motor vehicle is currently or was formerly titled or who last purchased a license tag or decal for the vehicle.
Person means every natural person, firm, partnership, association, corporation, trust, or other form of recognized business entity in the State of Georgia, including governmental authorities, but excludes a federal agencies, the state and its agencies, counties, municipal corporations, and school districts.
